{"id": "229d9658-4cb6-4769-a90c-e13685076f96", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "This is really more of a config audit than deep troubleshooting, so it's bounded in scope. Still, it needs multiple API calls — listing endpoints, checking config, model details, CloudWatch metrics, autoscaling — so I'll delegate this to a sub-agent to gather everything.

I don't know the exact endpoint yet, so I'll let the sub-agent discover it via listing, and have it check associations across accounts since the agent's own account/region might not be the only one involved. I'll preload skills for metrics exploration, log searching, and doc verification, then write a quick plan message to the user before delegating.

"}]}

{"id": "d4cd784f-83f6-4e10-b3b6-61df3e36a075", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll review your async inference endpoints' configuration. That covers the endpoint config, the async settings (output and failure paths, SNS notifications, concurrency limits), the autoscaling policy, and the model container's timeouts and payload limits. I'll compare these against the queue and invocation metrics, so I can tell you which settings could explain the dropped requests and the backlog.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_iEkcwwFlbiPWqnbfrMvbxJ", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "sagemaker-async-posture-review", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["exploring-metrics", "searching-logs", "verifying-with-docs"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Review the configuration posture of the SageMaker asynchronous inference endpoint(s) serving an LLM and identify what is misconfigured that could cause silently dropped requests and queue backlog.",
  "context": "User reports their SageMaker async inference endpoint for an LLM 'drops requests silently and sometimes the queue backs up'. They want a posture review listing misconfigurations. This is a bounded config audit (not an open-ended RCA). Agent space account is 123456789012, region us-east-1; use list_associations if other accounts/regions are associated and check them as well. First discover endpoints: list_endpoints and identify those whose endpoint config has AsyncInferenceConfig (describe_endpoint_config). If multiple async endpoints exist, prioritize ones that look LLM-related (name, model, GPU instance type e.g. ml.g5/p4/inf2) and report on all briefly.",
  "resources": ["SageMaker endpoints / endpoint configs / models with AsyncInferenceConfig", "Application Auto Scaling scalable targets & policies for the endpoint variant", "CloudWatch alarms on the endpoint", "SNS topics / S3 output and failure paths referenced in the config", "CloudWatch log group /aws/sagemaker/Endpoints/<name>"],
  "timeframe": "Last 7 days for metrics/logs (current time 2026-11-20T05:50:07Z)",
  "criteria": "Check and report on, with concrete values: (1) ClientConfig.MaxConcurrentInvocationsPerInstance vs. what the LLM container can actually handle (GPU memory, model server concurrency); (2) OutputConfig: S3OutputPath, S3FailurePath set?, NotificationConfig SuccessTopic/ErrorTopic/IncludeInferenceResponseIn set? SNS topic existence, subscriptions, policies/encryption (KMS) that could block delivery; S3 bucket existence/permissions/KMS issues for the execution role (read-only inspection); (3) Variant config: instance type/count, InitialInstanceCount, ContainerStartupHealthCheckTimeoutInSeconds, ModelDataDownloadTimeoutInSeconds, InvocationTimeout (ResponseTimeout) settings of the container/model server (e.g. SAGEMAKER_MODEL_SERVER_TIMEOUT, TS_* / DJL env vars), payload size limits; (4) Autoscaling: is there a scalable target with min capacity 0 or 1? Is policy based on ApproximateBacklogSizePerInstance (correct metric for async) vs. CPU/Invocations? Target value, scale-in/out cooldowns, step-scaling with HasBacklogWithoutCapacity; (5) CloudWatch metrics: ApproximateBacklogSize, ApproximateBacklogSizePerInstance, ApproximateAgeOfOldestRequest, HasBacklogWithoutCapacity, InvocationFailures, InvocationsProcessed, RequestsNotificationFailures? (check what exists), TimeInQueue, ModelLatency, plus instance GPU/memory utilization; note when backlog grew and if capacity was zero or instances were scaling; (6) Missing alarms for backlog/age/failures; (7) Endpoint logs: OOM, timeout, CUDA errors, 413/payload errors, worker restarts, failed health checks; (8) request expiry: note async requests have max 1 hour invocation timeout (InvocationTimeoutSeconds, default 3600) and max 1GB payload and verify configured values; also check whether the request EXPIRATION/queue retention could silently drop requests. Use verify_aws_claim for any doubtful limit/defaults. Read-only operations only. Return a concise prioritized list of misconfigurations/risks (severity, evidence with actual values, recommended fix) and note anything you couldn't check due to missing permissions. Also suggest deeper follow-up areas."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Review SageMaker async endpoint config and metrics"}], "created_at": null}

